# Accessibility

- Native elements first; ARIA only when semantics are insufficient. One `h1` per page, logical heading order, landmarks labelled when repeated, real lists, `<time datetime>` for dates.
- Every icon-only control has an accessible name; decorative SVGs are `aria-hidden`. Visible label text must be contained in the accessible name (2.5.3).
- Targets at least 44×44 CSS px (never below 24×24). Every drag has a single-pointer and keyboard alternative. Shortcuts use modifiers.
- Visible `:focus-visible` ring (2px `accent-2`, offset 2px), never hidden by the header or the terminal window. No keyboard traps except true modal dialogs (use native `<dialog>` + `showModal()`).
- Contrast: body text 7:1 (`text-1`, `text-2`), other text 4.5:1, UI and focus 3:1. `src/styles/tokens.test.ts` guards the tokens; don't put `text-3` on new surfaces without extending it.
- Motion: honor `prefers-reduced-motion` and the site's "Pause animations" toggle (`data-motion='reduced'`). No flashing above 3 Hz; anything moving longer than 5 s can be paused.
- Also honor `prefers-contrast: more`, `forced-colors: active` (add the `decorative` class to purely decorative layers) and `prefers-reduced-transparency`.
- Polite live regions for toasts, filter results, copy confirmations, terminal output and tech-cloud captions. Tooltips are dismissible with Esc, hoverable and persistent.
- Content stays fully visible without JavaScript (SSR renders visible; animations attach after hydration).
- Verify with `@axe-core/playwright` (WCAG 2.0/2.1/2.2 A+AA + best practices): zero violations.
